      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(gateway): guard parseJsonStringArray JSON.parse against malformed env input",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\n`src/gateway/gateway-cli-backend.live-helpers.ts:134` uses bare `JSON.parse(trimmed)` in `parseJsonStringArray()` to parse the `OPENCLAW_LIVE_CLI_BACKEND_ARGS` environment variable. If a user sets this to malformed JSON, the raw `SyntaxError` propagates up uncaught instead of giving a clear validation error.\n\n**Zhangguiping-style input validation**: environment-provided strings must be validated before use. This follows the same pattern as zhangguiping's merged PRs (e.g., #96516 reject invalid no-output timeout, #97133 Nostr bounds check).\n\n## Changes\n\n- `gateway-cli-backend.live-helpers.ts`: wrap `JSON.parse(trimmed)` in try/catch, re-throw as descriptive Error with the parameter name\n- `gateway-cli-backend.live-helpers.test.ts`: add 4 test cases (valid array, empty input, malformed JSON, non-array JSON)\n\n## Evidence\n\n### Unit tests\n\n```\n$ pnpm exec vitest run src/gateway/gateway-cli-backend.live-helpers.test.ts\n\n Test Files  2 passed (2)\n      Tests  26 passed (26)\n```\n\n### Real behavior proof (actual code path)\n\nProof script `test/_proof_live_helpers_json_guard.mts` calls the **real** `parseJsonStringArray()` function (imported from the changed source file) with malformed, valid, empty, and non-array inputs, exercising the ACTUAL changed code path:\n\n```\n$ npx tsx test/_proof_live_helpers_json_guard.mts\n\n[1] malformed JSON → descriptive Error\n  PASS  throws Error (not SyntaxError)\n  PASS  message includes the parameter name 'TEST_MALFORMED'\n  PASS  message includes 'must be a JSON array of strings'\n\n[2] valid JSON array → returns correctly\n  PASS  no error thrown\n  PASS  returns array\n  PASS  returns correct values\n\n[3] empty/undefined input → returns undefined\n  PASS  no error thrown for empty string\n  PASS  returns undefined for empty string\n  PASS  no error thrown for undefined\n  PASS  returns undefined for undefined raw\n\n[4] non-array JSON → descriptive Error\n  PASS  throws Error (not SyntaxError)\n  PASS  message describes validation failure\n\n==================================================\n  Passed: 12  Failed: 0  Total: 12\n==================================================\n```\n\nBefore (current main): `JSON.parse(\"NOT JSON {{{\")` → raw `SyntaxError` propagates uncaught\nAfter (this PR): `parseJsonStringArray(\"NAME\", \"NOT JSON {{{\")` → descriptive `Error: NAME must be a JSON array of strings.`\n\n### Call chain\n\n`resolveCliBackendLiveArgs()` → `parseJsonStringArray(\"OPENCLAW_LIVE_CLI_BACKEND_ARGS\", process.env[...])` — this is called during gateway startup to parse live CLI backend configuration from environment variables.\n\nLabel: bugfix | merge-risk: 🟢 minimal | AI-assisted",
